## 5. Toolchain & Modernization Pipeline

The repository was migrated from legacy Qt4/GCC 4.x codebases to support modern toolchains:

| Module / Vector | Legacy Target (Qt4 / MinGW32) | Modern Target (Qt 5.15+ / UCRT64) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **ABI Runtime** | `MSVCRT.DLL` (Legacy Win32 subsystem) | `UCRT.DLL` (ISO C Standard Universal CRT) |
| **Widget Hierarchy** | Monolithic `QtGui/*` include models | Modular `QtWidgets/*` pipeline separation |
| **Header Layout** | `QDesktopServices::storageLocation()` | Deterministic `QStandardPaths::writableLocation()` |
| **Table Layout** | `QHeaderView::setResizeMode()` | Strict section mapping `setSectionResizeMode()` |
| **String Coercion** | Insecure `.toAscii()` truncation | Deterministic `.toLatin1()` / `.toUtf8()` |
| **Type Aliasing** | Explicit `(double*)&int64` casting | Safe pointer conversions & aliasing guards |

---

## 6. Deterministic Build Procedure

The project strictly compiles with the MSYS2 UCRT64 toolchain environment.

### 1. Toolchain Initialization

Ensure dependencies are available via the MSYS2 package manager:

```bash
pacman -Sy --noconfirm mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-gcc \
                       mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-make \
                       mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-qt5-base

```

### 2. Compilation via PowerShell

```powershell
# Set deterministic path isolation to avoid path collisions
$env:Path = "C:\msys64\ucrt64\bin;C:\Windows\system32;C:\Windows"

# Navigate into project target directory
cd XDBF

# Ingest and serialize Makefile rules
qmake-qt5.exe XDBF.pro

# Compile binary across thread pool
mingw32-make -j$(Get-CimInstance Win32_ComputerSystem | Select-Object -ExpandProperty NumberOfLogicalProcessors)

# Launch build output
.\release\xbox-xdbf-explorer.exe

```

